      "startMilliseconds": 65880,
      "endMilliseconds": 84159,
      "kind": "explanation",
      "text": "Underneath, the runtime uses two kinds of memory: temporary memory called the stack and dynamic memory called the heap, so declaring a variable is fundamentally a memory operation.",
